Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraPlane", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"7385a662-fc75-46d3-9452-99d479c6d04f"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraPlane"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraPlane", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "899fa256-f4e4-4b4d-915d-07ce18cef207"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the inert family of inclusion-minimal separating vertex sets in the zero \
distance-difference slab.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"81099d5f-6569-4371-b757-3fa42b0903b7"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraPlane"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraPlane", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["lo", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      StyleBox["hi", "TI"]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "28bff0fe-b9a8-4d8c-ae0c-3242abd3cd1e"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "uses the stated distance-difference window."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"a41f0ded-f394-4b1b-b84c-a6a62babb2a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomInfraPlane"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraPlane", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8cd1df78-b534-4304-8ba6-12368f3c0b81"],
 " samples the family on a graph, fixing the separating property. One \
representative is a vertex set, not a payload wrapper. The exact finite \
equidistant locus is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraPerpendicularBisector"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraPerpendicularBisector", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b79bc8bb-f2a6-4461-a2ed-7c46382eac2b"],
 ", which need not separate the anchors. These constructions can therefore \
have different empty/nonempty answers."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"620d36f4-8edd-4292-8bd2-149b3beaf259"]
}, Open  ]],

